% ============================================================================
% ADJ52 case-11 derived rulebook.
% Clinical area: adult pancytopenia workup with a bone-marrow atypical
% LYMPHOID infiltrate + monocytopenia + reticulin fibrosis (flow / molecular /
% cytogenetic studies pending). Differential is built from the IR alone — no
% answer is given. Every clause carries a % rationale + source + trust.
%
% NOTE: numeric/unit lab values from the IR were normalized to qualitative
% atoms so they satisfy the adj-lang IDENT grammar (no uppercase, no leading
% digit). Mapping used throughout:
%   patient_age(years(64))                 -> patient_age(over_50)
%   hemoglobin 12.4 (ref 13-17)            -> anemia(mild)
%   mcv 102 (ref 80-100)                   -> mean_corpuscular_volume(macrocytic)
%   platelet 108 (ref 150-450)             -> thrombocytopenia(present)
%   anc 0.8 (ref 1.5-8.0)                  -> neutropenia(present)
%   wcc 2.6 (ref 4.0-11.0)                 -> leukopenia(present)
%   strikingly low absolute monocyte count -> absolute_monocyte_count(strikingly_low)
%   esr 24 (ref 0-12)                       -> erythrocyte_sedimentation_rate(modestly_raised)
%   counts depressed ~3 months              -> cytopenia_chronicity(persistent_months)
% ============================================================================

% ===== PRIORS (base rates for a 64yo with persistent pancytopenia + marrow
% atypical lymphoid infiltrate) =====

% rationale: HCL is a rare chronic B-cell malignancy that classically presents
% with pancytopenia, monocytopenia, marrow reticulin fibrosis and an atypical
% lymphoid marrow infiltrate — the exact constellation here.
prior 0.18 for diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "Blood 2017;129(5):553 consensus guidelines; NCBI Bookshelf NBK586203" trust authoritative

% rationale: HCL variant is the nearest mimic — a separate WHO entity with
% leukocytosis and (importantly) preserved monocytes; kept on the differential.
prior 0.08 for diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia_variant)
  source "Orphanet 300878; PMC4382572 (HCL-V differential diagnosis)" trust authoritative

% rationale: SMZL is the canonical B-cell lymphoproliferative differential for a
% splenic/marrow-based small-B-cell infiltrate; can give cytopenias.
prior 0.08 for diagnosis(splenic_marginal_zone_lymphoma)
  source "PMC4382572 (HCL vs HCL-V vs SMZL differential); StatPearls NBK499845" trust authoritative

% rationale: T-LGL leukemia is an indolent lymphoid leukemia that infiltrates
% marrow interstitially and characteristically causes cytopenias (esp.
% neutropenia) — a plausible T/NK-lineage explanation for the atypical lymphocytes.
prior 0.08 for diagnosis(t_large_granular_lymphocytic_leukemia)
  source "PMC4188790; ScienceDirect LGL overview" trust authoritative

% rationale: MDS is the leading non-lymphoid cause of persistent pancytopenia
% with macrocytosis in an older adult; must be excluded.
prior 0.10 for diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "StatPearls NBK534126; MSD Manual MDS" trust authoritative

% rationale: primary myelofibrosis explains marrow reticulin fibrosis + cytopenias
% but is a myeloid (not lymphoid) clonal process.
prior 0.06 for diagnosis(primary_myelofibrosis)
  source "MSD Manual Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF)" trust authoritative

% ===== HAIRY CELL LEUKEMIA =====

% rationale: multilineage pancytopenia is one of the most common presentations of HCL.
contributes 2.0 from pancytopenia(present) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "NCBI Bookshelf NBK586203 (HCL — multilineage cytopenias)" trust authoritative

% rationale: an atypical lymphoid marrow infiltrate is the substrate of HCL
% (small-medium B-cells with pale cytoplasm infiltrating marrow).
contributes 2.5 from marrow_infiltrate(atypical_lymphocytes) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "Pathology Outlines lymphomahcl; NBK586203" trust authoritative

% --- CORRELATED MECHANISM: monocytopenia + marrow reticulin fibrosis are NOT
% independent. Both are signature downstream effects of the hairy-cell clone:
% monocytopenia is near-universal (~98%) in HCL, and the reticulin fibrosis is
% produced by hairy cells assembling a fibronectin matrix (the "dry tap").
% Grouped as one mechanism so the combined LR fires ONCE rather than
% double-counting one underlying disease process. ---
% mechanism hairy_cell_clone for diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia) lr 9.0 : absolute_monocyte_count(strikingly_low), marrow_finding(increased_reticulin_fibrosis)

% rationale: absence of splenomegaly is atypical for HCL (splenomegaly is the most
% common sign) but HCL without splenomegaly is well documented -> mild AGAINST only.
contributes 0.7 from exam_finding(no_splenomegaly) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "Blood Research case report PMC5503894 (HCL without splenomegaly)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a non-contributory smear with no circulating abnormal cells fits
% HCL, where hairy cells are often sparse/absent in blood (marrow-based disease).
contributes 1.3 from smear_finding(no_atypical_or_abnormal_circulating_cells) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "PMC12370212 (HCL diagnosed despite absence of hairy cells in blood)" trust authoritative

% ===== HAIRY CELL LEUKEMIA VARIANT =====

% rationale: HCL-V shares the atypical B-lymphoid marrow infiltrate.
contributes 2.0 from marrow_infiltrate(atypical_lymphocytes) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia_variant)
  source "PMC4382572 (HCL-V differential)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR — HCL-V characteristically PRESERVES monocytes
% (lacks the monocytopenia of classic HCL); a strikingly low monocyte count
% argues strongly AGAINST the variant.
contributes 0.2 from absolute_monocyte_count(strikingly_low) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia_variant)
  source "PMC4382572 (HCL-V lacks monocytopenia, unlike classic HCL)" trust authoritative

% rationale: HCL-V usually presents with leukocytosis, not leukopenia/pancytopenia
% -> the pancytopenic picture here argues mildly against the variant.
contributes 0.6 from pancytopenia(present) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia_variant)
  source "PMC4382572 (HCL-V: leukocytosis common; pancytopenia favors classic HCL)" trust authoritative

% ===== SPLENIC MARGINAL ZONE LYMPHOMA =====

% rationale: SMZL is a small-B-cell lymphoproliferative disorder that can infiltrate marrow.
contributes 1.8 from marrow_infiltrate(atypical_lymphocytes) to diagnosis(splenic_marginal_zone_lymphoma)
  source "StatPearls NBK499845; PMC4382572" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR — SMZL is defined by splenomegaly; a normal-sized
% spleen on CT and exam argues against it.
contributes 0.4 from exam_finding(no_splenomegaly) to diagnosis(splenic_marginal_zone_lymphoma)
  source "PMC4382572 (SMZL is a splenic disease — splenomegaly expected)" trust authoritative

% rationale: SMZL does not characteristically cause monocytopenia; the striking
% monocytopenia is not explained by SMZL -> mild AGAINST.
contributes 0.6 from absolute_monocyte_count(strikingly_low) to diagnosis(splenic_marginal_zone_lymphoma)
  source "PMC4382572 (monocytopenia is the HCL-specific feature, not SMZL)" trust inferred

% ===== T-LARGE GRANULAR LYMPHOCYTIC LEUKEMIA =====

% rationale: T-LGL infiltrates marrow interstitially with a lymphoid population.
contributes 1.8 from marrow_infiltrate(atypical_lymphocytes) to diagnosis(t_large_granular_lymphocytic_leukemia)
  source "PMC4188790 (T-LGL marrow interstitial infiltrate)" trust authoritative

% rationale: T-LGL characteristically causes neutropenia/cytopenias — fits the ANC.
contributes 2.2 from neutropenia(present) to diagnosis(t_large_granular_lymphocytic_leukemia)
  source "PMC7529498; PMC9732502 (T-LGL severe neutropenia)" trust authoritative

% rationale: T-LGL does not produce the dry-tap reticulin fibrosis of HCL; marked
% reticulin fibrosis is not a T-LGL feature -> mild AGAINST.
contributes 0.6 from marrow_finding(increased_reticulin_fibrosis) to diagnosis(t_large_granular_lymphocytic_leukemia)
  source "PMC4188790 (T-LGL infiltrate; fibrosis is not a defining feature)" trust inferred

% rationale: T-LGL does not cause the near-universal monocytopenia of HCL -> the
% striking monocytopenia is not explained by T-LGL.
contributes 0.7 from absolute_monocyte_count(strikingly_low) to diagnosis(t_large_granular_lymphocytic_leukemia)
  source "ScienceDirect LGL overview (monocytopenia is HCL-specific)" trust inferred

% ===== MYELODYSPLASTIC SYNDROME =====

% rationale: MDS is a leading cause of persistent pancytopenia in older adults.
contributes 2.0 from pancytopenia(present) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "StatPearls NBK534126 (MDS — refractory cytopenias)" trust authoritative

% rationale: macrocytosis (MCV 102) is a classic MDS clue (dysplastic erythropoiesis).
contributes 2.5 from mean_corpuscular_volume(macrocytic) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "Medscape MDS workup; MSD Manual MDS (macrocytic anemia)" trust authoritative

% rationale: stable cytopenias >= months is part of the MDS prerequisite criteria.
contributes 1.6 from cytopenia_chronicity(persistent_months) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "Medscape MDS workup (IWG: cytopenia >=6 months prerequisite)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR — MDS is a MYELOID disorder; an atypical LYMPHOID
% marrow infiltrate is not MDS and points away from a myelodysplastic process.
contributes 0.4 from marrow_infiltrate(atypical_lymphocytes) to diagnosis(myelodysplastic_syndrome)
  source "StatPearls NBK534126 (MDS = myeloid dysplasia, not a lymphoid infiltrate)" trust authoritative

% ===== PRIMARY MYELOFIBROSIS =====

% rationale: reticulin fibrosis on marrow is the defining lesion of PMF.
contributes 2.5 from marrow_finding(increased_reticulin_fibrosis) to diagnosis(primary_myelofibrosis)
  source "MSD Manual PMF (diagnosis by reticulin/trichrome stain)" trust authoritative

% rationale: PMF gives cytopenias as marrow is replaced by fibrosis.
contributes 1.4 from pancytopenia(present) to diagnosis(primary_myelofibrosis)
  source "MSD Manual PMF (anemia/cytopenias from marrow replacement)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR — PMF produces a leukoerythroblastic smear with
% teardrop cells and splenomegaly; this smear is non-contributory with no
% abnormal cells -> argues against PMF.
contributes 0.4 from smear_finding(no_atypical_or_abnormal_circulating_cells) to diagnosis(primary_myelofibrosis)
  source "MSD Manual PMF (leukoerythroblastosis + teardrop cells expected)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR — PMF classically has splenomegaly (extramedullary
% hematopoiesis); a normal spleen argues against it.
contributes 0.5 from exam_finding(no_splenomegaly) to diagnosis(primary_myelofibrosis)
  source "MSD Manual PMF (massive splenomegaly characteristic)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR — PMF is a myeloid clonal process; an atypical
% LYMPHOID infiltrate is not PMF.
contributes 0.4 from marrow_infiltrate(atypical_lymphocytes) to diagnosis(primary_myelofibrosis)
  source "MSD Manual PMF (myeloproliferative, not lymphoid)" trust inferred

% ===== NEXT STEP (confirmatory investigation) =====

% rationale: flow cytometry of the marrow lymphoid population is the first
% confirmatory step — HCL shows CD11c/CD25/CD103/CD123 with pan-B markers, and
% flow distinguishes HCL from HCL-V and SMZL.
prior 0.25 for next_step(flow_cytometry_immunophenotyping)
  source "Blood 2017;129(5):553 consensus; ScienceDirect (4-antigen flow panel)" trust authoritative
contributes 4.0 from marrow_infiltrate(atypical_lymphocytes) to next_step(flow_cytometry_immunophenotyping)
  source "PMC4382572 (flow distinguishes HCL/HCL-V/SMZL)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.5 from absolute_monocyte_count(strikingly_low) to next_step(flow_cytometry_immunophenotyping)
  source "Blood 2017;129(5):553 (monocytopenia -> suspect HCL -> immunophenotype)" trust authoritative

% rationale: BRAF V600E is the disease-defining molecular marker for HCL,
% present in nearly all classic HCL and virtually absent in its mimics; the
% molecular study already sent is best directed at BRAF V600E.
prior 0.15 for next_step(braf_v600e_mutation_testing)
  source "NEJM 2011 NEJMoa1014209; PMC4129051 (BRAF V600E disease-defining for HCL)" trust authoritative
contributes 3.5 from absolute_monocyte_count(strikingly_low) to next_step(braf_v600e_mutation_testing)
  source "PMC4129051 (monocytopenia + lymphoid infiltrate -> test BRAF V600E)" trust authoritative

% rationale: cytogenetics/karyotype is the directed next step if MDS is the
% explanation (defining cytogenetic abnormalities establish MDS).
prior 0.10 for next_step(marrow_cytogenetics_karyotype)
  source "StatPearls NBK534126 (cytogenetics establishes MDS)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.0 from mean_corpuscular_volume(macrocytic) to next_step(marrow_cytogenetics_karyotype)
  source "Medscape MDS workup (karyotype for dysplastic macrocytic cytopenias)" trust authoritative

% ===== UNCERTAINTIES (decision-relevant, unresolved — pending flow/molecular) =====

% u3: lineage of the atypical marrow lymphocytes is unresolved pending flow.
% Resolving it (B vs T vs NK) moves the lymphoid differential.
uncertain { lineage(b_lymphocyte), lineage(t_lymphocyte), lineage(nk_cell) } for diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "Flow cytometry on marrow lymphocyte population (pending)"
% rationale: a B-cell phenotype with bright CD25/CD103/CD123 confirms classic HCL.
contributes 6.0 from lineage(b_lymphocyte) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "Blood 2017;129(5):553 (classic HCL B-cell immunophenotype)" trust authoritative
% rationale: a T-cell phenotype redirects toward T-LGL and away from HCL.
contributes 0.2 from lineage(t_lymphocyte) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "PMC4188790 (T-lineage -> T-LGL, not HCL)" trust inferred

% u: the molecular result (BRAF) is the disease-defining confirmation, unresolved.
uncertain { molecular(braf_v600e_present), molecular(braf_wild_type) } for diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "NEJM 2011 NEJMoa1014209 (BRAF V600E pending)"
% rationale: BRAF V600E present is near-diagnostic for classic HCL.
contributes 8.0 from molecular(braf_v600e_present) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "PMC4129051; NEJM 2011 (BRAF V600E nearly all classic HCL)" trust authoritative
% rationale: BRAF wild-type argues against classic HCL (favors HCL-V / mimic).
contributes 0.3 from molecular(braf_wild_type) to diagnosis(hairy_cell_leukemia)
  source "PMC3342983 (BRAF wild-type in HCL-V and related disorders)" trust authoritative
